{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels","id":1510468,"title":"It's Time to D-D-D-Crossover Arcane Duels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-02T00:40:48-07:00","id":1510468,"title":"It's Time to D-D-D-Crossover Arcane Duels","content":"Perhaps my google-fu is weak, but I am surprised that in a post Dark Eras 2 world, there hasn't been a thread, or really even posts, on Arcane Duels with non-mage sorts, and it goes double in a post-Contagion Player's Guide world.<br /> <br /> So yeah, let's just chat about what it takes to make a duel with all of the other splats happen-or perhaps, less the allowance, since that's basically just Mysterious Frontiers section on Changelings in the Duel Arcane plus the Arcana section of the Contagion PG, and more &quot;What features of the other splats would you use for their relative Sword and Shield?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll admit, there's no serious reason, so we probably don't need to be hard thinkers on this, but hell if we don't try for reasonably useful answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T02:05:40-07:00","id":1510474,"title":"","content":"I thought 2e removed Swords and Shields, though? Shame, since I want them.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we need some sort of tiered powers here\u2026 werewolves and their Renowns are low hanging fruit. So are vampires and Disciplines. Sineaters can use the Attributes linked to the Keys they have. Mummies have Pillars.<br /> <br /> The others are tougher to think of. Hunters? Demons? Beasts? Deviants? The latter can do something with Scars I imagine, but my Deviant-mastery is shaky still. Gonna have to think more after I finish jogging.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Hmm, Prometheans could use Transmutations that are dot-tiered by number of Alembics.<br /> Funnier idea; they use Alembics as is, but they can raise an Alembic\u2019s dot-ratings for the DA by charging Pyros as usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-02-2023, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T03:03:21-07:00","id":1510477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510474#post1510474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought 2e removed Swords and Shields, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, though for some reason <i>Mysterious Frontiers</i> refers to them.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T05:56:47-07:00","id":1510483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510477#post1510477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, though for some reason <i>Mysterious Frontiers</i> refers to them.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it\u2019s one of those purely in-universe flairs, then!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More ideas on the original topic: Beasts could use Atavisms. In-family ones as 4-dots, and out-of-Family ones as 2-dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T10:14:37-07:00","id":1510495,"title":"","content":"I double checked, and yep, no swords or shields. Let's figure out what correlates to Arcanum rating and how.<br /> <br /> On Beast,I had the initial thought of correlating to Lair and Saitety, but it does strike me as as a bit overpower given Satiety. I also feel like Nightmares need particular consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T12:39:55-07:00","id":1510515,"title":"","content":"I had considered Nightmares, but I didn\u2019t think they would have any ratings that wasn\u2019t arbitrary. Maybe it could be based on how close the nightmare is to the symbol of their Horror? No, that\u2019s too subjective. Oh wait. What if Satiety did have an effect? What if you qualify for the low or high Satiety effect, it buffs the Nightmare or Atavism to a higher rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T13:12:35-07:00","id":1510520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510515#post1510515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had considered Nightmares, but I didn\u2019t think they would have any ratings that wasn\u2019t arbitrary. Maybe it could be based on how close the nightmare is to the symbol of their Horror? No, that\u2019s too subjective. Oh wait. What if Satiety did have an effect? What if you qualify for the low or high Satiety effect, it buffs the Nightmare or Atavism to a higher rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I initially thought of Lair and Satiety, since Atavisms and Nightmares key off of each anyways and are actually ratable-but Satiety is easy to swing high, and also doesn't relate to the mastery aspect that keying off of Contracts and Arcana implies. The In-family/Out of family Dot Ranking is an interesting angle, but doesn't accomodate two thirds of a Beast's immediate demonstration of metaphysical mastery.<br /> <br /> Arguably, on that front, Chambers and Nightmares, particularly Kinship Nightmares, feels more like the sort of thing that would want to be tested against in an Awakened community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T13:29:28-07:00","id":1510521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510520#post1510520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I initially thought of Lair and Satiety, since Atavisms and Nightmares key off of each anyways and are actually ratable-but Satiety is easy to swing high, and also doesn't relate to the mastery aspect that keying off of Contracts and Arcana implies. The In-family/Out of family Dot Ranking is an interesting angle, but doesn't accomodate two thirds of a Beast's immediate demonstration of metaphysical mastery.<br /> <br /> Arguably, on that front, Chambers and Nightmares, particularly Kinship Nightmares, feels more like the sort of thing that would want to be tested against in an Awakened community.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the whole power set would be really. I don't know, a Thyrsus and a Kraken Makara dueling seems like it would get rather physical.<br /> <br /> Chambers are a good idea actually. What if associated Lair Tilts acted as dots? I forget if there is a max that can be on one Chamber though, might be too easy to get huge bonuses on it though.<br /> <br /> Duels are super metaphorical, right? I imagine a Beast has to first establish the &quot;Chamber&quot; the fight takes place in, then goes in with Nightmare and Atavism. Maybe acting in theme with the Chamber gives both sides a bonus or a penalty if they try and power through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T14:23:10-07:00","id":1510524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510521#post1510521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the whole power set would be really. I don't know, a Thyrsus and a Kraken Makara dueling seems like it would get rather physical.<br /> <br /> Chambers are a good idea actually. What if associated Lair Tilts acted as dots? I forget if there is a max that can be on one Chamber though, might be too easy to get huge bonuses on it though.<br /> <br /> Duels are super metaphorical, right? I imagine a Beast has to first establish the &quot;Chamber&quot; the fight takes place in, then goes in with Nightmare and Atavism. Maybe acting in theme with the Chamber gives both sides a bonus or a penalty if they try and power through.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing demonstrated with the Duel Arcane is what, exactly, one mage could do to another if they let loose-in basics, white room wizard dick measuring. The second major principle they work off is the value of mastery in mage society. the two are often mostly intertwined in Awakened society, but aren't strictly inter-related-a master who just raced to mastery is going to have less resources that a master who built up resources along the way to mastery, so on and so forth. And yes, it's loosely metaphorical (&quot;No, I would never break your knee in all 720 ways I could think of&quot;).<br /> <br /> Using Contracts as our measuring stick, changelings interact with the Duel Arcane in an odd way for both scores. It takes work to make the trade for a Royal Contract, but attaining one neither represents the sheer breadth of ability to dick over someone else, nor does it imply a particularly heightened mastery of the associated Regalia. Court Contracts fare better, but the attainment of related Mantle has more to do with living up to expectations of the Court Contract rather attaining a deeper understanding of it, which is closley associated but not the same thing again.<br /> <br /> of course, all of that presumes that mages or Supernal metaphysics actually care to cut the line that way. Instead, knowing a single Royal Contract is given the weight of being an Adept in the Regalia, breadth of ability or understanding be damned (and that's particularly important as it relates to both Spring and especially Autumn courtiers who put a premium on their understanding Wyrd magic, as opposed to Summer and Winter who may have dedicated sorcerers but aren't as invested in knowing the Wyrd's particular ins-and-outs, and on the whole hew material to Spring and Autumn's Mystical). Instead, the Duel Arcane seems to take it on faith that if you've negotiated for this one particularly costly thing, you could negotiate for similar, and execute them in ways that would suggest mastery.<br /> <br /> So the big thing for answering the question is both &quot;how would the wizard in question understand a creature's powers in both regards&quot; and &quot;does this make sense in the way Supernal metaphysics would translate them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2023, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T17:16:55-07:00","id":1510533,"title":"","content":"Rereading the content\u2026<br /> <br /> A changeling uses her Contracts in place of (pseudo-)spells, using either her Mantle ratings or the Regalia\u2019s assigned tier ratings depending on the Contract\u2019s type. Okay. Cool. <br /> <br /> What happens an Attack action in the Duel fails? Mages lose access to the entire Arcanum for the Duel; would changelings lose access to the entire Mantle/Regalia, or just that Contract? The former makes sense, but I want other opinions just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T17:28:01-07:00","id":1510535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510533#post1510533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading the content\u2026<br /> <br /> A changeling uses her Contracts in place of (pseudo-)spells, using either her Mantle ratings or the Regalia\u2019s assigned tier ratings depending on the Contract\u2019s type. Okay. Cool.<br /> <br /> What happens an Attack action in the Duel fails? Mages lose access to the entire Arcanum for the Duel; would changelings lose access to the entire Mantle/Regalia, or just that Contract? The former makes sense, but I want other opinions just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Regalia are the Arcana in this equation, with the individual contracts merely representing the &quot;level of mastery&quot; a changeling has within a Regalia (can't wait till my post gets reapproved), so likely it's the Regalia knocked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T19:14:29-07:00","id":1510542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510474#post1510474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The others are tougher to think of. Hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing or something appropriate provided by an Endowment \u2014 remember that &quot;a way to let hunters engage in the Duel Arcane&quot; outside of that context basically amounts to &quot;a way to let vanilla mortals engage in the Duel Arcane.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons? </div> </div> </div>Embed categories seems the direct option, though I'm currently struggling to figure out a way to provide more than one affinity that isn't inconsistent or messy as Hell \u2014 Incarnation affinity is relatively straightforward (albeit it leaves the Analysts out in the cold), but all my secondaries are either too easily acquired (&quot;any Embed category you've used an Embed from as the basis for learning an Exploit has an effective Arcanum rating of 4&quot;) or risks bad builds (&quot;count an Embed category you have a Key in as Arcanum 4&quot; runs afoul of the fact that you can have all four Keys be in-affinity or have Keys from all four categories, and &quot;add one to your effective Arcanum rating for each Key that comes from that Embed&quot; isn't much better).<br /> <br /> The most straightforward route, I think, would be that you treat each Embed category as an Arcanum with a rating based on how many Embeds you know from it (3 at four or more, 1 at only one, 2 for in-between) and can spend a point of Aether to add a die to it; your Incarnation adds 1 to your effective rating (Analysts instead get two bonus dice when spending Aether), and you also have a Cipher Arcanum whose rating is based on how many Keys you've found, which adds another die if you've gained a Beat from your Agenda Condition this chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts? </div> </div> </div>Minor and Major Lair Traits fit nicely into the 2/4 split pattern Regalia use and arguably serve as the template's closest analogue to Influence, and Chambers keying off of that makes for a solid way to further highlight the Begotten's personal triumphs in the Duel's contest of egos \u2014 maybe add an effective dot in the Arcanum for each step of Chamber similarity above Descriptive in the area and let the Beast use their Horror's Attributes as though the Duel was occurring within the Lair?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deviants? The latter can do something with Scars I imagine, but my Deviant-mastery is shaky still. Gonna have to think more after I finish jogging. </div> </div> </div>As with Hunter, but replace &quot;vanilla mortals&quot; with &quot;extremely broadly-manifested soul-explosion.&quot; Vampires at least have <i>convergent</i> evolution going for them in their codification scheme, but two deviants can have the same Clade and the same Scars and still be completely thematically different<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, Prometheans could use Transmutations that are dot-tiered by number of Alembics.<br /> Funnier idea; they use Alembics as is, but they can raise an Alembic\u2019s dot-ratings for the DA by charging Pyros as usual. </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Refinements as Arcana scaled by completed Roles, since that amounts to the same thing but feels tidier and allows for weird outcomes once calcification and Athanors come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T19:32:29-07:00","id":1510543,"title":"","content":"The biggest thing about Deviants is that the easiest take is also conflicted by how it should interact with itself, first by simply suggesting &quot;insert highest magnitude Variation in for Arcana&quot;, which quickly makes more sense as &quot;strength of the Scar implemented in the Duel&quot;, because of how Variations are grouped under Scars-but either one of those feels like the Scar should impediment them in some way. Perhaps any time a Deviant switches between Scars in a duel, tt should preceded by some kind of Acclimation roll to see how well they control the Scar and it's associated powers, with the Arcanum rating being the result of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T19:37:25-07:00","id":1510544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510535#post1510535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Regalia are the Arcana in this equation, with the individual contracts merely representing the &quot;level of mastery&quot; a changeling has within a Regalia (can't wait till my post gets reapproved), so likely it's the Regalia knocked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>And same for the Mantle, I presume.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves in the Duel Arcane</b><br /> <br /> <b>Renowned Arms</b>: A werewolf uses Renown in place of Arcana, using Gift Facets linked with it as individual \u2018spells\u2019. <br /> <br /> <b>Lunar Arms\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</b>: Each Moon Gift counts as a separate Renown for purposes of failed Attacks removing the used Arcanum.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<b>Regeneration</b>: If a werewolf Defends, and the opponent fails her Attack, the werewolf can regain access to an \u2018Arcanum\u2019 she lost from her own failed Attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Victory</b>: The Triumphant Condition works between mages and werewolves alike. A werewolf victor with Triumphant acquires perfect awareness of the loser\u2019s location, automatically succeeding Tracking rolls. <br /> <br /> (Forgot how Triumphant and Defeated worked exactly; gonna have to look up later\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T01:11:25-07:00","id":1510575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510533#post1510533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages lose access to the entire Arcanum for the Duel</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm reading it right, it's that you can't use the same arcanum against the <i>same door</i> if you fail. So once you're past that door you can go back to using which ever arcana you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T01:21:20-07:00","id":1510576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510575#post1510575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm reading it right, it's that you can't use the same arcanum against the <i>same door</i> if you fail. So once you're past that door you can go back to using which ever arcana you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I\u2019m away from my pdfs atm and had that from memory alone, so that could be more accurate.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, yeah \u2018refreshing\u2019 Arcana like that does make the Duel less likely to get locked in a stalemate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T15:44:37-07:00","id":1510646,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510524#post1510524\">that post</a> came back up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T19:02:23-07:00","id":1510656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510524#post1510524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">of course, all of that presumes that mages or Supernal metaphysics actually care to cut the line that way. Instead, knowing a single Royal Contract is given the weight of being an Adept in the Regalia, breadth of ability or understanding be damned ([\u2026]). Instead, the Duel Arcane seems to take it on faith that if you've negotiated for this one particularly costly thing, you could negotiate for similar, and execute them in ways that would suggest mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm moderately certain, looking at the mechanics from the future with the benefit of Kith and Kin, that it's related to the fact that you need at least one Royal Contract to be able to make a manifestation out of a Regalia.<br /> <br /> Given that Mantle aligns &quot;living up to expectations&quot; with &quot;becoming more like (your court's representation of) the court's patron,&quot; with court founders in particular needing to make thematic efforts to avoid having that change enforced as far as having their Clarity be the only thing keeping them from turning into a sockpuppet for Spring/Morning/North/etc, the commonality seems to be &quot;symbolic potency.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T19:05:43-07:00","id":1510657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1510468-it-s-time-to-d-d-d-crossover-arcane-duels?p=1510656#post1510656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm moderately certain, looking at the mechanics from the future with the benefit of Kith and Kin, that it's related to the fact that you need at least one Royal Contract to be able to make a manifestation out of a Regalia.<br /> <br /> Given that Mantle aligns &quot;living up to expectations&quot; with &quot;becoming more like (your court's representation of) the court's patron,&quot; with court founders in particular needing to make thematic efforts to avoid having that change enforced as far as having their Clarity be the only thing keeping them from turning into a sockpuppet for Spring/Morning/North/etc, the commonality seems to be &quot;symbolic potency.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely more accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}